                            {
                                "target_word": "Antonovka",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f508b8d7-a251-33e1-ba63-1f337ba4e6c9",
                                        "entry_id": "3b6b6f9c-7657-3c48-bcc7-be40d3878ee2",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An apple cultivar, noted for a strong acidic flavour and ability to sustain harsh winters."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "944b1c6f-ee55-4411-9cec-8256955ddb55",
                                                "sense_id": "f508b8d7-a251-33e1-ba63-1f337ba4e6c9",
                                                "text": "She looked at some apples, turned a few over, took a whiff of some others, but just couldn't make up her mind which to buy — it was as though her whole fate depended on it. She finally spied some golden ones with the fragrance of champagne — smooth round Antonovkas. And above them was the smiling, golden face of a Korean farmer."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c74cc734-31b9-4d0a-9f51-fcf5ce52f9b9",
                                                "sense_id": "f508b8d7-a251-33e1-ba63-1f337ba4e6c9",
                                                "text": "It was easy: a quick jump over a low stone wall, a dash past a few rows of berry bushes, and there it was— the cursed tree with its absurd apples. Large poison-green spheres with deeply scalloped bottoms: Antonovkas. They were a good eating apple, but Jarmo had no interest in them."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b8bb9ee2-b7eb-40d8-8b58-0ebd5c89cb6a",
                                                "sense_id": "f508b8d7-a251-33e1-ba63-1f337ba4e6c9",
                                                "text": "With the appearance of scab races 6 and 7, major attention has been focused on other scab resistance factors, particularly the “Antonovka” selections and apple genotype R12740-7A (“Russian seedling”, RS), which are currently used in several apple-breeding programs."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
